    {
      "sha": "82007dab239034024995f491e381940696a0e9a8",
      "message": "Cards: the derived 1NT rebid range under a 1NT opening from 13 or 14 (G9-B10 item 4)\n\nWhen a card does not state its 1NT rebid range, it was derived as the range above the 1NT opening whenever the\nopening started at 14 or lower: 17-17 for a 14-16 notrump, empty for 14-17. Now a 1NT opening from 13 or 14 with two\npoints or more below it gives the balanced minimum under it, as a strong notrump does: (11, 13) for 14-16 with 11-point\nopenings, (12, 13) for 14-17 with 12. Weak notrumps keep the range above.\n\nNo built-in card bids or reads differently: only rb-precision's derived range changes (17-17 to 11-13, which is what\nthe rule bidder it describes rebids 1NT with, balanced 11 to 13 on 175 of 6,000 deals), and its card does not cover\nrebids. Tests pin the built-in ranges; the card suites pass (68 passed, 3 skipped). The card-intake report's note,\nwhich said the fix would change rb-precision's calls, is corrected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N2EvxCJBUzzHdcpohDTBew",
      "parents": [
        "576014ca1c8400ff93d8cc6f01ebafe11f2c9d37"
      ],
